<div class="offcanvas offcanvas-end" data-bs-scroll="true" tabindex="-1" id="offcanvasWithBothOptions"
    aria-labelledby="offcanvasWithBothOptionsLabel">
    <div class="offcanvas-header">
        <h5 class="offcanvas-title" id="offcanvasWithBothOptionsLabel">Help</h5>
        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="offcanvas" aria-label="Close"></button>
    </div>
    <div class="offcanvas-body">
        <p>Read more about the interactive algorithm visualization tool for the Traveling Salesman Problem here.</p>
        <ul class="nav nav-tabs" id="myTab" role="tablist">
            <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                <button class="nav-link active" id="home-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#home-tab-pane"
                    type="button" role="tab" aria-controls="home-tab-pane" aria-selected="true">Settings</button>
            </li>
            <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                <button class="nav-link" id="profile-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#profile-tab-pane"
                    type="button" role="tab" aria-controls="profile-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">Graph</button>
            </li>
            <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                <button class="nav-link" id="contact-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#contact-tab-pane"
                    type="button" role="tab" aria-controls="contact-tab-pane" aria-selected="false">Contact</button>
            </li>
            <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                <button class="nav-link" id="disabled-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#disabled-tab-pane"
                    type="button" role="tab" aria-controls="disabled-tab-pane" aria-selected="false" disabled>Disabled</button>
            </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="tab-content" id="myTabContent">
            <div class="tab-pane fade show active" id="home-tab-pane" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="home-tab" tabindex="0">
                <br/>
                <p>In the <em>dropdown menu</em> you can choose between Nearest Neighbor, Simulated Annealing, Ant Algorithm,
                    Hill Climbing and Manual Search. The selection of the algorithm influences which parameters can be configured in the
                    heuristic settings area.</p>
                <h5>Multi-Start</h5>
                <p>Additionally, the checkbox <em>Multi-Start</em> can be activated for Nearest Neighbor and Hill-Climbing.
                    Instead of running the algorithm once, it will be run n times, depending on the number of nodes in the graph.</p>
                <h5>Starting tour</h5>
                <p>Simulated Annealing, Hill Climbing and Manual Search improve a tour, so they need one to start from. By
                    default that is the order the nodes are listed in. To state a different one, add a line
                    <code>t,index,index,&hellip;</code> to the graph text, listing every node once in visiting order. It may be
                    written open or closed; anything that is not a tour of the given nodes is rejected with the reason.</p>
                <h5>Manual Search</h5>
                <p>Plays the search by hand: you choose each move yourself instead of letting a rule choose it. Pick the move
                    type, pick the nodes it applies to, and the panel shows what the move would cost <em>before</em> it is
                    applied - so a calculation done on paper can be checked against it. <em>Apply Move</em> adds it to the move
                    history, and moves of different types can be chained in any order.</p>
                <p>The two canvases show the tour before and after the last move, the distance matrix stands next to the move
                    history so the edge lengths can be read off, and each row of the history carries the calculation that move
                    actually used. <em>Undo</em> takes the last move back; stepping to an earlier state and applying something
                    else replaces the continuation from there, so different lines of play can be compared.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tab-pane fade" id="profile-tab-pane" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="profile-tab" tabindex="0">
                ...
            </div>
            <div class="tab-pane fade" id="contact-tab-pane" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="contact-tab" tabindex="0">
                ...
            </div>
            <div class="tab-pane fade" id="disabled-tab-pane" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="disabled-tab" tabindex="0">
                ...
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

